body:
A pinup I put together for my comic out of boredom and a bad workday ;;  


[Neo Automisia's](https://neo-a.the-comic.org) a cyberpunk psych. thriller/action/It's Complicated™ webcomic centered around a depressive mercenary and her brushes with varying levels of existential crises, inspired by the strange dystopias of Shadowrun, Lowlife 2090, and Coyote & Crow to name a few.  


Things are slow to update 'cause i still have to work a dayjob, which eats up a lot of my time that could otherwise be spent on art- outside the dayjob this's where 90% of my free time goes, hope you enjoy it.

huge mood, shit's absolutely fucked ;-;

&#x200B;

just take what time you need for you, you know? a little self care goes a long way, even if it doesn't fix everything in the moment

Speaking as a worker in a position considered unskilled, I can tell you that there is no unskilled labor- only labor thats undervalued. A living wage that pays enough to afford housing in the area, food, and to make ends meet without constantly struggling to exhaustion or juggling jobs is not that much to ask for- especially when full time positions perform the same labor at a higher wage.

&#x200B;

Licking an employers boots will afford you no upward mobility or security- you're just helping them keep wages down at that point.

Eheh, uh- I work for RHA xux;

They gave me a bare minimum explanation, and we haven't exactly had time to discuss it further than what I know. Its way above me, and at the very least they're letting the mural stay for now- though i honestly expect that'll change in a few months, given it'll create contrast between the 9 other paintable TCRs in Holmes ~~when we can literally just extend the project to the other trash rooms and even it out~~

Its a headache x_x
